\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf {The odd-offset shifts are one subtraction.} PREPARE (left) puts the offset register $d$ in a uniform superposition over the $N/2$ odd offsets, by an $X$ on its lowest qubit and Hadamards on the rest. SELECT is a ripple-carry subtractor \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {cuccaro2004adder} that replaces the system register $p$ by $p-d$ and sets the borrow flag when $p<d$. PREPARE$^\dagger $ (right) with post-selection of $d$ and the borrow flag on $\mathinner {|{0}\rangle }$ keeps $\tfrac {2}{N}\mathinner {|{k}\rangle }\!\mathinner {\langle {p}|}$ for every odd $d=p-k\ge 1$, and the wrapped terms vanish exactly. The block is $U_{\mathrm {odd}}/(N/2)$, so $\alpha =N/2$, on $n$ system and $n+2$ ancilla qubits.}}{17}{figure.caption.29}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Dense against banded: the two residuals of the same equation.}}{22}{figure.caption.32}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The descriptor block encoding: one PREPARE/SELECT/PREPARE$^\dagger $ over the whole residual.}}{29}{figure.caption.43}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Model configuration: from problem specification to decoded field.}}{34}{figure.caption.55}%
